course: dictionary
lesson: 3542
title: Feebly and weak words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Feebly is an adverb. It tells you how someone does something. It means weakly, without much strength or energy.
explain: «Without them Toad is just Toad again, and he giggles feebly.» Toad is not laughing loudly. He giggles in a small, weak way, so feebly tells you how he giggles.
explain: Look at the words around feebly for clues. A kitten that mews feebly is too weak to make a loud sound. Alice speaks feebly when she is confused or afraid, so she sounds unsure. To check, swap in weakly: "he giggles weakly" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Feebly is an adverb, a word that tells how something is done.
fact: «Feebly» means weakly, without much strength or energy.
fact: «Feebly» can also mean in a poor, unconvincing way, as in «he laughed feebly at the joke».
fact: People often speak or move feebly when they are ill, tired, frightened or unsure.
fact: The adjective is feeble, and feebly is its adverb form.
exercise: «Without them Toad is just Toad again, and he giggles feebly.» How does Toad giggle? | At the top of his voice | *Weakly, with little energy | Loudly and happily | Very fast
exercise: «The kitten mewed feebly.» What does feebly show about the kitten? | *It was weak, with very little strength | It was fast asleep | It was singing a song | It was strong and angry
exercise: «He laughed feebly at the joke.» What does feebly suggest? | *In a poor, unconvincing way | With a big smile that everyone loved | Quickly, like a runner | Very loudly and proudly
test: Alice speaks feebly when she is confused. What does feebly tell you about Alice? | *She sounds unsure and weak | She is laughing | She is sure of every word | She is shouting
test: Which sentence shows feebly meaning unconvincing? | *He said he was fine, but he said it feebly, and nobody believed him | She lifted the box feebly, with her arms shaking | The bell rang feebly far away | The dog barked feebly, too sick to get up
exam: What does feebly mean in «the kitten mewed feebly»? | *Weakly, with little strength | Happily | Quickly | Loudly
